                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Runs well on Steam Deck, despite not ‘Steam Deck Verified’ and listed as Unsupported[/h1]\n\nI picked this up for a couple of bucks in my local currency, and it looks like a really fun game. It combines Pandas, and apparently Robots, in a 2D platformer. Warm cosy fun. Very nostalgic of an NES game. I’m liking it so far, but it had a few hurdles.\n\n[b]If playing in Steam Deck, or Steam Machine, follow these guidelines[/b]\n(*) Do not change the controller settings in settings. It already works, and you will break it.\n(*) When you first play, you will THINK only the jump button (A) works, and it is borked. Please select the TUTORIAL option, which will show you the mechanics\n(*) Attack (x) only works if you have a weapon. Finding your training sword is part of the journey. Likewise, you will be able to shoot (b). But again, you have to find the weapons first. So PLAY THE TUTORIAL ALREADY\n(*) To find the sword, you will need to leave the first area and go into the forest. You can’t beat the whole level, return to village.\n\n\nThe rest I leave you to explore and enjoy. But don’t discount this game - it is really quite fun. It’s simple, but has an RPG progression element as well, so it’s worth persevering with.",
